//@check

// Multiple bases will lead to the compilation getting ambiguous or no
// references to symbols it needs, so we must disregard all global diagnostics.
//@ignore-global-diagnostics

// Namespaces are open only across the same compilation and
// must not redeclare namespaces of dependencies. This is mainly
// to avoid merging logic in my Compilation :D. But it also
// seems sound.

// Currently, only Base can be referenced (honestly, I don't know if
// that is going to change).

//---
namespace Base;     //~error NamespaceAlreadyDeclared

//---
namespace Base;     //~error NamespaceAlreadyDeclared